{"title":"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of integers has a sum of 420, and an average of 60. If one of the integers in the set is 120, what is average of the remaining integers in the set?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of numbers, including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Since there is a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb2fec2f1cde0059d8eb9c11bcb2bd63142401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9d064923eca16d9854fb898afc915f50e2b6f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{420}{n} = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114e2a97353f0058236abbf53acc191650cca611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{420}{60} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee068e9ec1a1408fec805621db65ada911fda40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> numbers without that specific value. The sum of the numbers without <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> would also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6c453ead0f66b2ce58de5b5ee2fbcf4e61cd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420 - 120 = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The new average would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46ab2a86c966af9d993a01933d4c2957324c7c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{300}{6} = \\boxed{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1806/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.574      1 2012_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.574      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36048:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230401 and revision id 279734. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}